messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-mcore.c
Line: 418
Function: coff_mcore_relocate_section
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The relocation symbol index rel->r_symndx is used without bounds checking to index multiple arrays. At line 418, obj_coff_sym_hashes(input_bfd)[symndx] dereferences with an unvalidated symndx; at lines 419–421 and 438 it is also used to compute syms + symndx and sections[symndx]. A crafted object file with an invalid (negative other than -1, or too-large) r_symndx can cause out-of-bounds reads and crashes.

Source context:
